{"id":"mikro","name":"Pi & Mikrocontroller","untertitel":"GPIO, PWM, ADC, Boards","farbe":"#a6e22e","symbol":"quarz","reihenfolge":8,"seiten":[{"id":"gpio","titel":"Raspberry Pi GPIO-Leiste","kurz":"40-Pin-Header anklicken: Funktion, Alternativfunktionen","tags":["gpio","pi","raspberry","pinout","header","40 pin","bcm","40","pin","i2c","spi","uart","pwm","stiftleiste","2×20","(40-Pin)","40-pin","belegung"],"bloecke":[{"t":"text","text":["Klicke auf einen Pin, um Funktion, Nummer (BCM/Board) und Alternativfunktionen zu sehen. **Alle GPIOs arbeiten mit 3,3 V**, nicht 5 V-tolerant!"]},{"t":"spezial","name":"gpio"},{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["Funktion","BCM-Pins","Board-Pins"],"zeilen":[["I²C1 (SDA, SCL)","GPIO2, GPIO3","3, 5"],["SPI0 (MOSI, MISO, SCLK, CE0, CE1)","10, 9, 11, 8, 7","19, 21, 23, 24, 26"],["UART0 (TX, RX)","GPIO14, GPIO15","8, 10"],["PWM0 / PWM1","GPIO12/18 · GPIO13/19","32/12 · 33/35"],["1-Wire (Standard)","GPIO4","7"],["PCM / I2S (BCLK, LRCLK, DIN, DOUT)","18, 19, 20, 21","12, 35, 38, 40"]],"mono":[],"fett":true},{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["Grenzwert","Wert"],"zeilen":[["Spannung an GPIO","3,3 V (nicht 5 V!)"],["Strom pro Pin","max. 16 mA (empfohlen ≤ 8 mA)"],["Strom gesamt (alle GPIO)","ca. 50 mA"],["3,3-V-Pin","ca. 50–500 mA (Gesamtlast beachten)"],["5-V-Pin","Rest vom Netzteil minus Pi (ca. 1,5 A)"],["Pull-Up/Down intern","ca. 50 kΩ"]],"mono":[],"fett":true},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"pi","text":"Mit Pi 5 heißt die Bibliothek `gpiod`/`gpiozero`; **RPi.GPIO funktioniert auf Pi 5 nicht** (anderer Chip RP1). Nutze `gpiozero` oder `lgpio`."},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"warn","text":"Nie 5 V auf einen GPIO-Eingang legen, nie 2 Pins mit unterschiedlichem Pegel kurzschließen. Bei Unsicherheit **Pegelwandler** (BSS138-Modul)."},{"t":"h2","text":"Pinbelegung der 40-poligen Stiftleiste"},{"t":"text","text":["Alle Funktionen des Pi-Anschlusses: Versorgung, GPIOs und Sonderfunktionen (I²C, SPI, UART, PWM). 3,3-V-Logik!"]},{"t":"bauteil","e":{"id":"pi-gpio","name":"Raspberry Pi GPIO (40-Pin)","titel":"Pinbelegung der 40-poligen Stiftleiste (Pi 3 / 4 / 5 / Zero 2)","kurz":"Alle Funktionen des Pi-Anschlusses: Versorgung, GPIOs und Sonderfunktionen (I²C, SPI, UART, PWM). 3,3-V-Logik!","familie":"Raspberry Pi","gehaeuse":"Header 2×20","pins":["3V3:v","5V:v","GPIO2·SDA1:x","5V:v","GPIO3·SCL1:x","GND:g","GPIO4:x","GPIO14·TXD:x","GND:g","GPIO15·RXD:x","GPIO17:x","GPIO18·PWM:x","GPIO27:x","GND:g","GPIO22:x","GPIO23:x","3V3:v","GPIO24:x","GPIO10·MOSI:x","GND:g","GPIO9·MISO:x","GPIO25:x","GPIO11·SCLK:x","GPIO8·CE0:x","GND:g","GPIO7·CE1:x","ID_SD:n","ID_SC:n","GPIO5:x","GND:g","GPIO6:x","GPIO12·PWM:x","GPIO13·PWM:x","GND:g","GPIO19·MISO:x","GPIO16:x","GPIO26:x","GPIO20:x","GND:g","GPIO21:x"],"spannung":"GPIO 3,3 V (NICHT 5-V-tolerant).","hinweise":["Links die ungeraden Pins (1, 3, 5 …), rechts die geraden (2, 4, 6 …). Pin 1 (3V3) ist oben links, wenn die SD-Karte unten liegt.","Jeder GPIO ist nur mit 3,3 V belastbar. Maximal ca. 16 mA pro Pin, insgesamt etwa 50 mA – größere Lasten über Transistor / MOSFET.","I²C-1: GPIO2 (SDA), GPIO3 (SCL) – hat schon 1,8-kΩ-Pull-ups auf der Platine. SPI-0: GPIO10 / 9 / 11, CE0 = GPIO8, CE1 = GPIO7. UART: GPIO14 (TX), GPIO15 (RX).","Hardware-PWM: GPIO12 / 13 / 18 / 19. Pins 27/28 (ID_SD / ID_SC) sind für HAT-EEPROMs reserviert.","Pi 5: der Header hängt am RP1-Chip – bei gpiod/gpiozero zeigt `gpiodetect`, welche Chip-Nummer er hat (meist gpiochip4 bzw. gpiochip0 in neueren Kernen)."],"tags":"raspberry pi gpio header 40 pin i2c spi uart pwm pinout stiftleiste","kerbe":false,"oben":"Pin 1 oben links","kat":"module","uid":"module:pi-gpio"}},{"t":"h2","text":"Alle 40 Pins als Tabelle"},{"t":"text","text":["Der 40-polige Header (Pi 3/4/5, Zero). Linke Spalte = ungerade Pins (außen am Rand der Platine), rechts gerade. **BCM** ist die GPIO-Nummer, die in Software (gpiozero, pinctrl) gilt."]},{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["Pin","Name","Art","BCM","Pin","Name","Art","BCM"],"zeilen":[["1","3V3","3,3 V","–","2","5V","5 V","–"],["3","GPIO2 SDA","GPIO","2","4","5V","5 V","–"],["5","GPIO3 SCL","GPIO","3","6","GND","GND","–"],["7","GPIO4","GPIO","4","8","GPIO14 TXD","GPIO","14"],["9","GND","GND","–","10","GPIO15 RXD","GPIO","15"],["11","GPIO17","GPIO","17","12","GPIO18 PWM","GPIO","18"],["13","GPIO27","GPIO","27","14","GND","GND","–"],["15","GPIO22","GPIO","22","16","GPIO23","GPIO","23"],["17","3V3","3,3 V","–","18","GPIO24","GPIO","24"],["19","GPIO10 MOSI","GPIO","10","20","GND","GND","–"],["21","GPIO9 MISO","GPIO","9","22","GPIO25","GPIO","25"],["23","GPIO11 SCLK","GPIO","11","24","GPIO8 CE0","GPIO","8"],["25","GND","GND","–","26","GPIO7 CE1","GPIO","7"],["27","GPIO0 ID_SD","GPIO","0","28","GPIO1 ID_SC","GPIO","1"],["29","GPIO5","GPIO","5","30","GND","GND","–"],["31","GPIO6","GPIO","6","32","GPIO12 PWM","GPIO","12"],["33","GPIO13 PWM","GPIO","13","34","GND","GND","–"],["35","GPIO19","GPIO","19","36","GPIO16","GPIO","16"],["37","GPIO26","GPIO","26","38","GPIO20","GPIO","20"],["39","GND","GND","–","40","GPIO21","GPIO","21"]],"mono":[0,3,4,7],"fett":true,"titel":"Header-Belegung"},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"warn","text":"GPIO-Pins vertragen **3,3 V**. 5 V an einem Eingang kann den Pi zerstören (Spannungsteiler oder Pegelwandler benutzen). Pro Pin maximal ca. 16 mA, insgesamt wenige 10 mA."}],"siehe":["pwm","schnittstellen:i2c","mcu:v_pegel"],"symbol":"gehaeuse"},{"id":"pwm","titel":"PWM & Timer","kurz":"Tastverhältnis, Frequenz, Auflösung","tags":["pwm","tastverhältnis","duty","timer","dimmen","servo","frequenz"],"bloecke":[{"t":"text","text":["**PWM** (Pulsweitenmodulation) schaltet ein Signal schnell ein und aus. Das **Tastverhältnis** (Duty Cycle) bestimmt den Mittelwert: 25 % an → im Mittel 25 % der Spannung."]},{"t":"formel","name":"Mittelwert und Frequenz","f":"U_mittel = U · D        f = 1 / T        D = t_ein / T","text":""},{"t":"rechner","titel":"PWM-Rechner","felder":[["u","Spannung","V","3,3"],["d","Tastverhältnis","%","25"],["f","Frequenz","Hz","1k"]],"ergebnis":[["um","Mittelwert","u*d/100","V"],["t","Periodendauer","1/f","s"],["ton","Einschaltzeit","d/100/f","s"]]},{"t":"rechner","titel":"Timer → PWM-Frequenz (AVR / Arduino)","felder":[["fcpu","CPU-Takt","Hz","16M"],["pre","Vorteiler","","64"],["n","Zählerbreite (Bits)","","8"]],"ergebnis":[["f","PWM-Frequenz (Fast PWM)","fcpu/(pre*2**n)","Hz"]]},{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["Anwendung","Frequenz","Hinweis"],"zeilen":[["LED-Dimmen","500 Hz – 20 kHz","> 100 Hz flimmerfrei, > 20 kHz unhörbar"],["Servo","50 Hz","1–2 ms"],["DC-Motor","1–20 kHz","unhörbar > 20 kHz"],["Lüfter (4-Pin)","25 kHz","Intel-Spec"],["Netzteil (Buck)","100 kHz – 2 MHz","Schaltfrequenz"],["Audio-DAC (PWM)","> 100 kHz + Filter","Tiefpass nötig"]],"mono":[],"fett":true},{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["Pi-Hardware-PWM","Pins"],"zeilen":[["PWM0 Kanal 0","GPIO12, GPIO18"],["PWM0 Kanal 1","GPIO13, GPIO19"]],"mono":[],"fett":true,"titel":"Hardware-PWM (stabil), Rest per Software"},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"tipp","text":"Mit PWM-Pins dimmt man **LED-Streifen** über einen MOSFET. Auflösung mit 8 Bit = 256 Stufen, 10 Bit = 1024, 12 Bit = 4096."},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"warn","text":"PWM an induktiven Lasten (Motor): Freilaufdiode nicht vergessen und Frequenz oberhalb des Hörbereichs wählen, sonst **pfeift** der Motor."}],"siehe":["halbleiter:mosfet","sensoren:motoren"],"symbol":"sinus"},{"id":"adc","titel":"ADC & DAC","kurz":"Auflösung, LSB, Referenz, Abtasttheorem","tags":["adc","dac","auflösung","mcp3008","ads1115","abtast","nyquist","analog"],"bloecke":[{"t":"formel","name":"Auflösung (LSB)","f":"LSB = U_ref / 2ⁿ","text":""},{"t":"formel","name":"Messwert","f":"Code = U_in / U_ref · (2ⁿ − 1)","text":""},{"t":"rechner","titel":"ADC-Rechner","felder":[["u","Eingangsspannung","V",""],["ur","Referenz","V","3,3"],["n","Bits","","12"],["c","ADC-Code","","2048"]],"formeln":{"u":["c/(2**n-1)*ur"],"c":["u/ur*(2**n-1)"]},"text":"Lass ein Feld leer – es wird aus den anderen berechnet. Schreibweise: 4k7, 10u, 2,2M, 100n."},{"t":"rechner","titel":"Auflösung","felder":[["ur","Referenz","V","3,3"],["n","Bits","","12"]],"ergebnis":[["lsb","1 LSB","ur/2**n","V"],["s","Stufen","2**n","","ganz"]]},{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["ADC","Bits","Kanäle","Schnittstelle","Hinweis"],"zeilen":[["Arduino Uno intern","10","6","–","0–5 V"],["ESP32 intern","12","18","–","nicht linear!"],["Pico intern","12","3 + Temp","–","ENOB ≈ 9"],["MCP3008","10","8","SPI","Pi-Standard, günstig"],["MCP3208","12","8","SPI",""],["ADS1115","16","4","I²C","mit PGA, differentiell"],["ADS1015","12","4","I²C","schneller"]],"mono":[],"fett":true},{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["DAC","Bits","Schnittstelle"],"zeilen":[["MCP4725","12","I²C"],["MCP4921","12","SPI"],["PCM5102","32 (Audio)","I²S"]],"mono":[],"fett":true,"titel":"DAC-Bausteine"},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"merke","text":"**Abtasttheorem (Nyquist):** Abtastrate f_s > 2 · f_max des Signals. Sonst entstehen **Aliasing**-Fehler (falsche Frequenzen). Bei Audio: 44,1 kHz für 20 kHz."},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"pi","text":"Der Pi hat **keinen ADC**. Nimm MCP3008 (SPI) oder ADS1115 (I²C) oder lass einen Pico/Arduino die analogen Messwerte liefern."}],"siehe":["passiv:ntc","schnittstellen:spi"],"symbol":"voltmeter"},{"id":"takt","titel":"Takt, Baudrate & Zeit","kurz":"Teiler, Timer, Baudraten-Fehler","tags":["takt","baudrate","uart","timer","teiler","frequenz","prescaler"],"bloecke":[{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["Baudrate","Bit-Dauer","Bytes/s (8N1)"],"zeilen":[["9600","104,2 µs","960"],["19200","52,1 µs","1 920"],["38400","26,0 µs","3 840"],["57600","17,4 µs","5 760"],["115200","8,68 µs","11 520"],["230400","4,34 µs","23 040"],["921600","1,085 µs","92 160"],["1 000 000","1 µs","100 000"]],"mono":[],"fett":true,"titel":"UART (8 Datenbits, kein Paritätsbit, 1 Stopbit = 10 Bits pro Byte)"},{"t":"rechner","titel":"UART-Übertragungszeit","felder":[["b","Baudrate","","115200"],["n","Bytes","","1000"]],"ergebnis":[["t","Dauer (10 Bits/Byte)","n*10/b","s"],["bps","Nutzdaten","b*8/10","Bit/s"]]},{"t":"rechner","titel":"Baudratenfehler (AVR)","felder":[["f","CPU-Takt","Hz","16M"],["b","Baudrate","","115200"]],"ergebnis":[["ubrr","UBRR (gerundet)","round(f/(16*b)-1)","","zahl"],["real","Tatsächliche Baudrate","f/(16*(round(f/(16*b)-1)+1))","","zahl"],["err","Fehler","(f/(16*(round(f/(16*b)-1)+1))-b)/b","","proz"]]},{"t":"formel","name":"Timer-Überlauf","f":"T = (2ⁿ · Vorteiler) / f_CPU","text":"Für 16 Bit, 16 MHz, Vorteiler 1024: 4,19 s."},{"t":"rechner","titel":"Timer","felder":[["f","CPU-Takt","Hz","16M"],["n","Zählerbits","","16"],["p","Vorteiler","","1024"]],"ergebnis":[["t","Überlaufzeit","2**n*p/f","s"],["fo","Überlauf-Frequenz","f/(2**n*p)","Hz"]]},{"t":"tabelle","kopf":["Fehler UART","Bewertung"],"zeilen":[["< 2 %","in Ordnung"],["2–3 %","grenzwertig"],["> 3 %","Übertragungsfehler wahrscheinlich"]],"mono":[],"fett":true},{"t":"hinweis","typ":"tipp","text":"Probleme mit Zeichenmüll (zufällige Zeichen) auf der seriellen Schnittstelle: **Baudrate falsch**, Pegel falsch (5 V ↔ 3,3 V) oder TX/RX nicht gekreuzt."}],"siehe":["passiv:quarz","schnittstellen:uart"],"symbol":"quarz"}]}